<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Evaluation Metrics</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the formal definitions of the evaluation metrics used in our experiments, including Recall@k, NDCG@k, and Mean Reciprocal Rank (MRR).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a query <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, let the reranker output an ordered list of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> candidates <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{q}=(c_{1},\ldots,c_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{q}=(c_{1},\ldots,c_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, sorted by decreasing predicted relevance score.
Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ground-truth relevance label of candidate <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for query <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (1 for relevant, 0 for non-relevant).
Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the (1-indexed) position of the highest-ranked relevant candidate:</p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}_{q}=\min\{i\mid y_{i}=1\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}_{q}=\min\{i\mid y_{i}=1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}_{q}=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}_{q}=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> if no relevant candidate exists in the list.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Recall@k.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall@k measures whether at least one relevant candidate is retrieved within the top-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> results:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Recall@}k(q)=\mathbb{I}\big[\min_{1\leq i\leq k}y_{i}=1\big]=\mathbb{I}\big[\mathrm{rank}_{q}\leq k\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mi>@</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Recall@}k(q)=\mathbb{I}\big[\min_{1\leq i\leq k}y_{i}=1\big]=\mathbb{I}\big[\mathrm{rank}_{q}\leq k\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function.
We report the average Recall@k over all queries:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Recall@}k=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{Recall@}k(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Recall@}k=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{Recall@}k(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">MRR</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MRR measures how early the first relevant candidate appears:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{RR}(q)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\mathrm{rank}_{q}},&amp;\mathrm{rank}_{q}&lt;+\infty,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>RR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>rank</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{RR}(q)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{\mathrm{rank}_{q}},&amp;\mathrm{rank}_{q}&lt;+\infty,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and Mean Reciprocal Rank averages this quantity over queries:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(20)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MRR}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{RR}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MRR</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>RR</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MRR}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{RR}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">NDCG@k.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">NDCG@k evaluates ranked-list quality with position-based discounting.
We first define DCG@k for a query as:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(21)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DCG@}k(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{2^{y_{i}}-1}{\log_{2}(i+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>DCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DCG@}k(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{2^{y_{i}}-1}{\log_{2}(i+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We then compute the ideal DCG@k by sorting candidates by ground-truth relevance:</p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(22)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)=\max_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{2^{y^{\pi}_{i}}-1}{\log_{2}(i+1)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>IDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>π</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)=\max_{\pi}\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{2^{y^{\pi}_{i}}-1}{\log_{2}(i+1)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> ranges over permutations and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{\pi}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{\pi}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the relevance label at position <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, NDCG@k is the normalized form:</p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(23)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NDCG@}k(q)=\begin{cases}\frac{\mathrm{DCG@}k(q)}{\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)},&amp;\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)&gt;0,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>NDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>DCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>IDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>IDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NDCG@}k(q)=\begin{cases}\frac{\mathrm{DCG@}k(q)}{\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)},&amp;\mathrm{IDCG@}k(q)&gt;0,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We report mean NDCG@k across queries:</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{NDCG@}k=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{NDCG@}k(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>NDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>NDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{NDCG@}k=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{NDCG@}k(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All metrics are computed on the reranked top-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> list produced by the reranker given the candidate set returned by the first-stage retriever.
In our experiments, we report <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,3,5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,3,5\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Dataset Construction Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Scientific Literature Retrieval</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the scientific domain on the <span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MMDocIR</span> benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which targets multimodal information retrieval over long documents.
MMDocIR provides two retrieval granularities: page-level retrieval and fine-grained layout-level retrieval, where a <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">layout</em> corresponds to a localized region such as a paragraph, figure, or table.
In this work, we focus on the <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">layout-retrieval</em> setting in the <em id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Academic Paper</em> domain, where each document is a visually rich scientific paper with structured layouts, citations, and academic figures/tables.
Given a text-only question, the system retrieves and reranks the top-<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> most relevant layout regions within the document.
As reported by MMDocIR, the evidence layouts in the Academic Paper domain span multiple modalities, including text, image, and table regions, making it a representative testbed for hybrid-candidate reranking.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For evaluation, we directly use the Academic Paper subset from the MMDocIR evaluation set.
Figure <a href="#A2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ B.1. Scientific Literature Retrieval ‣ Appendix B Dataset Construction Details ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates a representative layout-level reranking example, where a text-only query is matched against hybrid candidate regions (paragraphs, figures, and tables) within a scientific paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For training our reranker, we use the MMDocIR training set and focus on its <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SciQAG</span> subset (scientific papers) to construct in-domain reranking supervision.
Specifically, we form query–candidate pairs from MMDocIR-provided layout-level labels and split them into the supervised fine-tuning set <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the hold-out set <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{hold}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>hold</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{hold}}</annotation></semantics></math> (used for hard-negative mining and preference data construction).
Additional examples of the instruction format and preference instances are provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Prompt Templates and Training Data Examples ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.29897v1/mmdocir_example.png" id="A2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/189;" width="405" height="189" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>Example from MMDocIR Academic Paper (layout-retrieval).
Given a text-only question, the retriever/reranker selects the most relevant layout regions (e.g., paragraph/figure/table) within a long scientific document.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.29897v1/ruiguan_example.png" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:405/189;" width="405" height="189" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3. </span>Example from the design patent search task.
Given a target product as the query (image + text), the reranker scores and orders multiple recalled design patents (candidates) by infringement risk.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Design Patent Search</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Task definition.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The design patent search task is motivated by real-world product appearance risk screening.
Given a <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">target product</em> as the query and a set of recalled <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">comparison patents</em> as candidates, the goal is to judge whether the product and each patent are <em id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">substantially similar</em> in overall visual impression and output a reranking score for sorting the candidate patents.
Each query corresponds to multiple candidate patents, and the reranker is evaluated on its ability to place high-risk (similar) patents above low-risk (dissimilar) ones.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Candidate retrieval.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each target product, we first retrieve a candidate pool of potentially similar design patents using an off-the-shelf appearance-based retrieval system.<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                
                
                
              <a href="https://open.eric-bot.com/docs" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://open.eric-bot.com/docs</a></span></span></span>
This step provides the initial candidate set for reranking and simulates the standard retrieve-then-rerank pipeline in deployment.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Labeling with a large multimodal model.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To construct supervision signals for reranker training, we assign binary risk labels to each product–patent pair using <span id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gemini-3-pro-preview</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
Concretely, for each query, we provide the model with

<span id="A2.I1" class="ltx_inline-enumerate">
<span id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_inline-item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_inline-item">(1)</span> <span id="A2.I1.i1.2" class="ltx_text">the target product’s main image and optional textual fields (title/description), and
</span></span>
<span id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_inline-item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_inline-item">(2)</span> <span id="A2.I1.i2.2" class="ltx_text">each candidate patent’s structured metadata (e.g., title, abstract, specification text, and patent identifier) together with representative patent figures.
</span></span>
</span>
The model is instructed to compare the two designs from an overall-appearance perspective and returns a structured prediction that includes a risk label.
We then treat the predicted risk label as the supervision signal for reranker training and evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset construction for reranking.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After labeling, we construct a standard reranking dataset where each query (product) is paired with its recalled candidates (patents) and corresponding risk labels.
We create the supervised fine-tuning set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}</annotation></semantics></math> from labeled query–candidate pairs, reserve a disjoint subset as <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{hold}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>hold</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{hold}}</annotation></semantics></math> for hard-negative mining and preference construction, and use a held-out test split for final evaluation.
Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ B.1. Scientific Literature Retrieval ‣ Appendix B Dataset Construction Details ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> illustrates the reranking setup in this domain, where a target product query is compared against multiple recalled design patents.
Examples of our system prompts, SFT instances, and preference pairs for this domain are provided in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Prompt Templates and Training Data Examples ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section summarizes the key implementation details of <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">UniRank</span>, including training hyperparameters and computational cost.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Training Configuration</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement both SFT and GRPO-based RLHF using the <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Swift</span> framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
All experiments are conducted with parameter-efficient fine-tuning via LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2022</a>)</cite> on top of <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-VL-*</span> backbones.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameters.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Hyperparameters. ‣ C.1. Training Configuration ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Hyperparameters. ‣ C.1. Training Configuration ‣ Appendix C Implementation Details ‣ UniRank: End-to-End Domain-Specific Reranking of Hybrid text-image Candidates" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> list the hyperparameters used for SFT and GRPO, respectively.
Unless otherwise stated, we keep hyperparameters fixed across domains.</p>
</div>
